@*
    THE LIST'S OWN SHAPE WHILE IT LOADS — shared partial (owner report, 2026-09-21).

    ⚠ WHY A SHAPE AND NOT FIVE BARS. A skeleton's only job is to say "something of THIS shape is coming". The
    five generic bars every list used to draw said nothing: the same five bars appeared whether the answer was a
    table, a panel or a tree, and they sat ABOVE the real table header, so when the data arrived the toolbar and
    the pager popped in underneath and the page grew downwards. The owner's words: "anlaşılmıyor, sayfa geldikten
    sonra yukarıdan aşağı yükleniyor." The Role Permissions screen already does this right — its skeleton is
    shaped like its own panels — and that is the half of it worth copying.

    ⚠ NO NEW SKELETON LANGUAGE (backbone-custom.css). The blocks are still `.shimmer` + `.skeleton-row`, the
    product's only placeholder vocabulary. Everything added here is LAYOUT — where those same blocks sit so the
    group reads as a toolbar, a header, rows and a footer. A second animation or a second grey would be the
    thing that warning forbids.

    ⚠ IT IS VISIBLE FROM THE SERVER'S FIRST PAINT, AND THAT IS THE WHOLE MECHANISM. It carries no
    `.backbone-skeleton` (which hides), so it is on screen before a single line of JavaScript has run — which is
    when a placeholder is actually needed. The CSS beside it hides the real table for as long as this element is
    a sibling, and `dt-defaults.js` REMOVES this element once the table has drawn; the table then appears
    because its selector no longer matches.

    ⚠ WHY NOT A LOADING HOOK. The first version asked DataTables to show it from a `preXhr` option — and
    DataTables has no such option (`preXhr` is an EVENT; its registered init callbacks are drawCallback,
    initComplete, preDrawCallback, rowCallback and the state ones, measured in the vendored source). That
    function was never called once, on any page, which is why the owner still saw the spinner. A placeholder
    that depends on nothing cannot fail that way.

    ⚠ `data-table-skeleton` IS THE OPT-IN: a list still carrying the old hidden block keeps its old behaviour
    exactly, and nothing is migrated by surprise.
*@
<div id="skeleton-loader" class="dt-skeleton p-4" data-table-skeleton aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="dt-skeleton-toolbar">
        <span class="shimmer skeleton-row dt-skeleton-search"></span>
        <span class="shimmer skeleton-row dt-skeleton-button"></span>
        <span class="shimmer skeleton-row dt-skeleton-button"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="shimmer skeleton-row dt-skeleton-head"></div>
    @for (var row = 0; row < 6; row++)
    {
        <div class="dt-skeleton-row">
            <span class="shimmer skeleton-row dt-skeleton-cell dt-skeleton-cell--sm"></span>
            <span class="shimmer skeleton-row dt-skeleton-cell dt-skeleton-cell--lg"></span>
            <span class="shimmer skeleton-row dt-skeleton-cell"></span>
            <span class="shimmer skeleton-row dt-skeleton-cell dt-skeleton-cell--sm"></span>
        </div>
    }
    <div class="dt-skeleton-footer">
        <span class="shimmer skeleton-row dt-skeleton-info"></span>
        <span class="shimmer skeleton-row dt-skeleton-pager"></span>
    </div>
</div>
